      "kind": "faq",
      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>Is a safety data sheet a COSHH assessment?</h3><p>No. HSE says a good safety data sheet does not substitute for carrying out and recording a COSHH risk assessment. The sheet describes the product. The assessment covers your use of it.</p><h3>Which parts of the sheet matter most for COSHH?</h3><p>The hazard and labelling sections, the exposure controls and protective equipment, and the first aid, fire, spill and disposal sections.</p><h3>Can Quickler fill a COSHH form from a safety data sheet?</h3><p>Yes. You send the sheet as a file in WhatsApp and say how the product is used. Quickler fills your COSHH Check from both. You then read and correct the Record.</p><h3>Does Quickler decide whether the controls are enough?</h3><p>No. It records what the sheet says and what you tell it. A competent person decides whether the controls are suitable.</p><h3>Do I need to type the sheet in?</h3><p>No. Send the file. Quickler reads it.</p>"
    }
